`sumNumericLeaves(value)` recursively sums finite numeric leaves in arrays and plain objects. Empty arrays and objects contribute zero. `null`, strings, booleans, functions, symbols, bigints, non-finite numbers, and non-plain objects must throw `TypeError("Unsupported value.")`. A plain object has prototype `Object.prototype` or `null`. Property traversal follows ordinary `Object.values` order. Inputs must not be mutated. Cyclic input is outside the API contract.

Known-bad source:

```typescript
export function sumNumericLeaves(value: unknown): number {
  if (typeof value === "number") {
    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) throw new TypeError("Unsupported value.");
    return value;
  }
  if (Array.isArray(value)) {
    return value.reduce<number>((sum, item) => sum + sumNumericLeaves(item), 0);
  }
  if (typeof value === "object") {
    const prototype = Object.getPrototypeOf(value);
    if (prototype !== Object.prototype && prototype !== null) {
      throw new TypeError("Unsupported value.");
    }
    return Object.values(value).reduce<number>(
      (sum, item) => sum + sumNumericLeaves(item),
      0,
    );
  }
  throw new TypeError("Unsupported value.");
}
```

